WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
K: We are looking together at the whole movement of consciousness, not as an idea to be accepted, but as a fact that each human being can observe directly in daily relationship. Observation begins when authority, conclusion, and personal preference no longer dictate what the mind is permitted to discover for itself.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Thought has accumulated experience, knowledge, memory, and response, and from that background it projects an image of tomorrow while interpreting the living present through what has already happened. When this movement is seen without condemnation or justification, attention can remain with the fact and learn how division is continually produced.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The observer then discovers that it is not separate from the thing observed, because both the observer and its reactions arise from the same stored memories and inherited patterns. This is not a verbal conclusion, and therefore it demands patient attention to fear, pleasure, ambition, comparison, and every subtle form of escape.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
In such attention there is no centre directing experience toward a chosen result, so the mind is quiet without discipline, suppression, or the promise of a future reward. That quietness has its own intelligence, and from it action may occur immediately, without the conflict created by opposing fragments of desire.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Please examine this in your own life rather than following the description, because the description is never the actuality and the word is never the thing. A mind that sees this distinction clearly can meet relationship anew, without carrying yesterday as the measure of every encounter today.
